WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.440
welcome to the David Pakman show.

00:00:01.440 --> 00:00:06.589
I am Farron cousins from Maria buyer sitting
in once again today for David Packman and

00:00:06.589 --> 00:00:07.589
today I wanted

00:00:07.589 --> 00:00:12.030
to start the show with a little bit of good
news because most of the stuff we have to

00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:14.639
discuss as either terrifying were depressing.

00:00:14.639 --> 00:00:17.990
So let's begin with something positive.

00:00:17.990 --> 00:00:25.519
And the positive comes in the form of new
poll numbers showing that roughly 40% of expected

00:00:25.519 --> 00:00:35.881
voters for 2020 40% rate climate change as
a top issue, not the top issue, but 40% say

00:00:35.881 --> 00:00:41.030
that they are strongly going to consider a
candidate stance on climate change before

00:00:41.030 --> 00:00:47.579
casting a ballot in 2020 and that is up 5%
from the 2016 numbers.

00:00:47.579 --> 00:00:54.050
When only about 35% of the country said that
climate change was going to impact their vote.

00:00:54.050 --> 00:00:55.390
So those numbers are going up.

00:00:55.390 --> 00:01:03.850
They're going up slowly, but they are up and
that is always a positive 40% it's not even

00:01:03.850 --> 00:01:04.850
half.

00:01:04.850 --> 00:01:07.930
I understand that, but that is encouraging.

00:01:07.930 --> 00:01:12.530
Finally, we have at least 40% of the country
as a whole.

00:01:12.530 --> 00:01:18.130
The eligible voters as a whole who understand
that climate change is one of the most important

00:01:18.130 --> 00:01:21.940
issues facing this country today.

00:01:21.940 --> 00:01:25.840
Not any of these made up scenarios from politicians.

00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:27.750
It's not the threat of Irfan.

00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:30.490
It's not the threat of people coming across
the border.

00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:35.090
It's an actual real threat that scientists
have been warning us about for decades.

00:01:35.090 --> 00:01:37.980
And that is obviously climate change.

00:01:37.980 --> 00:01:42.479
Now the numbers get a little bit skewed when
you break it down by party.

00:01:42.479 --> 00:01:51.909
Um, you, uh, with the Democrats, you have
about 76% say that climate change is important

00:01:51.909 --> 00:01:55.890
to their vote, a little over 30% for independence.

00:01:55.890 --> 00:02:01.370
And then of course we're hovering around 10%
for Republicans.

00:02:01.370 --> 00:02:06.510
Those numbers on the lower end, obviously
not exactly what we want to see, but we can

00:02:06.510 --> 00:02:13.110
take a little bit of time to be happy about
the fact that hey, at least 10% of Republicans

00:02:13.110 --> 00:02:15.700
say climate change is important.

00:02:15.700 --> 00:02:20.470
And to be honest, that that 10 to 12% is actually
pretty good.

00:02:20.470 --> 00:02:26.730
Considering the fact that conservative media
routinely tells us, tells their audience that

00:02:26.730 --> 00:02:31.970
climate change does not exist, that it's some
kind of liberal hoax, that the planets just

00:02:31.970 --> 00:02:38.230
in one of those warming slash cooling cycles
that happens, all the or that a snowball in

00:02:38.230 --> 00:02:43.870
DC somehow disproves what scientists had been
saying for decades.

00:02:43.870 --> 00:02:49.200
So 10% may seem small, but when you consider
the amount of misinformation that the right

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:57.160
absorbs on a daily basis, 10% ain't that bad,
folks, I think we should be happy about that.

00:02:57.160 --> 00:03:02.010
And here's the another reason why we need
to be happy about these 40% as a whole numbers.

00:03:02.010 --> 00:03:09.180
And that is because this is an issue that
we still have time to fix.

00:03:09.180 --> 00:03:13.630
Nothing is set in stone yet and that is one
of the big things that climate scientists

00:03:13.630 --> 00:03:17.990
have been encouraging people to talk about
when they talk about climate change.

00:03:17.990 --> 00:03:19.760
We can't talk all gloom and doom.

00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:20.760
We're done.

00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:21.760
The planet's dead.

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:25.770
No, they said we have to remind people that
there is still time.

00:03:25.770 --> 00:03:30.630
Because if we do talk in those terms of, Oh,
we've burned the planet down, nothing we can

00:03:30.630 --> 00:03:34.400
do, then yeah, people lose hope and they stopped
caring about it.

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:37.629
They just say, okay, well this is what it
is.

00:03:37.629 --> 00:03:38.629
Nothing I can do.

00:03:38.629 --> 00:03:39.629
I'm not going to change my ways.

00:03:39.629 --> 00:03:40.900
I'm not going to call for action.

00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:44.129
We're doomed, but that's not the truth.

00:03:44.129 --> 00:03:45.880
We have time.

00:03:45.880 --> 00:03:47.300
We have plenty of time.

00:03:47.300 --> 00:03:52.430
To be perfectly honest with you, it's just
that we have leaders in this country and other

00:03:52.430 --> 00:03:59.379
leaders abroad who were not doing enough and
it is our job to push them to do more, and

00:03:59.379 --> 00:04:05.510
that is why the 40% number is so important
because if we act fast, if we stay on top

00:04:05.510 --> 00:04:07.680
of this issue, we can do something about it.

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:15.150
We can change the future, but if we put another
climate change denier into the White House,

00:04:15.150 --> 00:04:19.669
if we put somebody in the White House who
is squarely in the pocket of the fossil fuel

00:04:19.669 --> 00:04:24.979
industry, the nothing's going to change and
we're going to lose another four years on

00:04:24.979 --> 00:04:26.650
this very important issue.

00:04:26.650 --> 00:04:29.400
We may not have four years to lose.

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:34.990
I know, uh, at the end of last year, we got
the report saying we had about 12 years before

00:04:34.990 --> 00:04:39.139
we see the irreparable damages from climate
change, but that's been six months.

00:04:39.139 --> 00:04:42.150
So we're at 11 and a half years now.

00:04:42.150 --> 00:04:44.539
Get that number 12 out of your brain.

00:04:44.539 --> 00:04:45.979
We've lost six months.

00:04:45.979 --> 00:04:47.599
We can make up for it.

00:04:47.599 --> 00:04:52.479
We have the technology costs of renewable
energy are now coming down.

00:04:52.479 --> 00:04:55.669
It's actually more affordable than fossil
fuels.

00:04:55.669 --> 00:04:58.009
We need the infrastructure in place.

00:04:58.009 --> 00:05:02.509
So look for that in candidates, especially
on the democratic side, obviously in their

00:05:02.509 --> 00:05:08.949
climate plans, because without that renewable
energy infrastructure, all the windmills,

00:05:08.949 --> 00:05:13.439
all the solar farms, all of that isn't going
to mean that much if we, if we do not have

00:05:13.439 --> 00:05:15.430
a viable delivery system.

00:05:15.430 --> 00:05:19.689
Now, that's another thing that a lot of people
don't seem to understand.

00:05:19.689 --> 00:05:21.990
It's like, yeah, just switched to renewables.

00:05:21.990 --> 00:05:25.759
We could have done that and we could have
built out this infrastructure 10 years ago,

00:05:25.759 --> 00:05:28.319
15 years ago, started building it out.

00:05:28.319 --> 00:05:31.099
But unfortunately that didn't happen.

00:05:31.099 --> 00:05:33.870
So we are behind the curve on this, right?

00:05:33.870 --> 00:05:38.569
We have lot of work to do, but those who are
saying that the technology simply doesn't

00:05:38.569 --> 00:05:39.569
exist.

00:05:39.569 --> 00:05:42.740
Or if you listen to the president who tells
you that, oh, when the wind doesn't blow and

00:05:42.740 --> 00:05:47.030
you're on wind power, you don't watch TV that
night, that's a lie.

00:05:47.030 --> 00:05:49.050
Battery capacity is up.

00:05:49.050 --> 00:05:57.539
Uh, delivery systems have evolved and if we
put them in place, we absolutely as a country

00:05:57.539 --> 00:05:59.999
could do this.

00:05:59.999 --> 00:06:04.289
We could have been a leader on this issue
of climate change and renewable energy, but

00:06:04.289 --> 00:06:10.020
instead we felt in the back of the pack and
we're now having to play catch up to all of

00:06:10.020 --> 00:06:15.460
the other countries in the world who are meeting
their emissions reduction marks while the

00:06:15.460 --> 00:06:19.930
US has blown way past hours.

00:06:19.930 --> 00:06:26.909
But 40% is a good number, not as good as we
would like it.

00:06:26.909 --> 00:06:32.339
But at this point you got to take every little
victory that you can and 40% saying climate

00:06:32.339 --> 00:06:48.149
change is going to influence

00:06:48.149 --> 00:07:37.940
their vote.

00:07:37.940 --> 00:08:37.529
That 
is a good number.

